      "name": "infer_replace_programs",
      "code": "def infer_replace_programs(inputs: list[str], outputs: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Infer a short sequence of replace programs (max 5, each with substrings \u22643 chars) that transforms each input string into the corresponding output string.\n    The function scans each input-output pair, identifies the minimal differing region, and builds unique replace commands.\n    \"\"\"\n    programs: list[str] = []\n    seen: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()\n    for inp, out in zip(inputs, outputs):\n        if inp == out:\n            continue\n        # find first differing index\n        i = 0\n        while i < min(len(inp), len(out)) and inp[i] == out[i]:\n            i += 1\n        # find last differing index\n        j_inp = len(inp)\n        j_out = len(out)\n        while j_inp > i and j_out > i and inp[j_inp - 1] == out[j_out - 1]:\n            j_inp -= 1\n            j_out -= 1\n        src = inp[i:j_inp]\n        tgt = out[i:j_out]\n        # enforce length \u22643, truncate if necessary\n        if len(src) > 3:\n            src = src[:3]\n        if len(tgt) > 3:\n            tgt = tgt[:3]\n        key = (src, tgt)\n        if key not in seen:\n            seen.add(key)\n            programs.append(f\"replace('{src}','{tgt}')\")\n        if len(programs) >= 5:\n            break\n    return programs",
      "description": "Infer a short sequence of replace programs to map inputs to outputs.",
      "domain": "symbolic_program_inference",
